{
  "dom_id": "step-q339125",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+5}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14189988/assets/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+5} & =\\frac{7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)}{(0)^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(0)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{5} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
